From ddd7234fa2e4ffde268aea04f61efc4f39e0dd5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:31:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: Add voltage-safe SC2 CPU and DSU sequencing

Wrap cpufreq-dt with the SC2 shared CPU/DSU clock sequence and the real
CPU regulator callback. Raise voltage before clock changes, park the
CPU while programming SYS PLL and switch DSU at the BSP thresholds.

Reject mutable video-PLL ancestry of the inherited PWM_J clock and
check actual output rates. Any uncertain clock transition latches both
callbacks against later voltage reduction. Do not register a separate
uncoordinated generic cpufreq-dt device on SC2.

Use the full exact stock OPP table with normal upstream policy, not an
invented initial floor or unproven SKU selection. Calibration, inherited
PWM state and firmware DSU rate support require combined acceptance.

Change-Id: Ie6a8a694f96aca80ead9190efcba369c9927857f
---
 drivers/cpufreq/Kconfig.arm          |   9 +
 drivers/cpufreq/Makefile             |   1 +
 drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c |   2 +
 drivers/cpufreq/sc2-cpufreq.c        | 291 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 303 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/cpufreq/sc2-cpufreq.c

